// Canonical Go identity module requirements (#2861, #2862).
//
// A go.mod FRAGMENT, not a module file: fold these require lines into the same
// go.mod you folded the ops-api payload's into, then `go mod tidy`. Place the
// payload's .go files into internal/identity/ FIRST -- tidy removes any
// requirement no package in the working tree imports, so run against a tree
// that does not yet contain them and it silently strips these lines and exits 0.
//
// ONE library per job, deliberately, with no alternative and no switch between
// libraries:
//
//   - go-oidc is the blessed Go OIDC validator: issuer discovery, a remote JWKS
//     key set that re-fetches on an unknown key (so a key rotation needs no
//     restart), and a verifier that checks iss, aud and exp with the signing
//     algorithms pinned by configuration. It brings go-jose in as its own
//     requirement; tidy writes that line, and nothing in this payload imports it.
//   - golang.org/x/oauth2 (its clientcredentials package) is the blessed
//     client-credentials token source for service-account calls (s2s.go): a
//     cached token, refreshed only on expiry.
//
// The versions are floors, not pins -- Renovate/Dependabot move them. Note the
// /v3 import path.

require github.com/coreos/go-oidc/v3 v3.21.0
require golang.org/x/oauth2 v0.37.0
